      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To recognize critical peaks, look for clustered non-verbal signals such as rapid changes in body language, fixed and intense eye contact among strangers, or an increase in sharp, clipped speech patterns. Pay attention to environmental cues like sudden pauses in background noise or an observable shift in foot traffic patterns becoming more agitated. These markers often precede a rapid escalation in collective mood.",
      "source": "target",
